				<wikidot:authorName>Monteparnas</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>2926286</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Page 1 is ok, it works pretty well establishing the setting.</p> <p>Page 2 is twofold. Ovum's description went well, but the dialogue between O5 and Clef is very poor. Clef is overall out of place.</p> <p>Page 3 could present Ovum with an actual plan about the gems, instead of just &quot;destroy it&quot;. It seems that Clef was essentially right about letting him with the thing. The end of the scene was excessively expunged.</p> <p>Page 4 is simply awful, and wasn't even necessary. You could expand 3 and collapse the picture there. But seriously, what an awful page. It breaks convention for no reason, adds nothing, explains nothing, it just throw random pieces of &quot;awesomeness&quot; without context.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
